9. Microphone Array Research Provenance
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The Microphone Array implementation was written independently for
Splitwave. No source code, tests, configuration files, or assets from
pyroomacoustics, ODAS, paderwasn, openMHA, or BeamformIt are included
or distributed.

Published GCC-PHAT, GSC, and MVDR papers and the public documentation
of those projects were studied as research and architecture references.
In particular, no AGPL-3.0 openMHA code and no BeamformIt code (whose
repository did not expose a license during the audit) was copied,
translated, or incorporated.

The feature adds no third-party runtime dependency. It uses the existing
permissively licensed `rubato`, `rtrb`, and `rustfft` dependencies under
the repository's cargo-deny policy. Full references and the provenance
table are in docs/microphone-array-architecture.md.
